# Machine-local agent tooling state, repo root (B5-0835, 2026-09-28).
# All four are per-machine tool state, never repo content. .mimocode already
# self-ignores its own node_modules and manifests; these root entries are
# belt-and-braces for a tool that rewrites or deletes that nested file, since
# an untracked nested .gitignore is itself invisible to git.
/.mimocode/

# .qwen/ and .freebuff/ are ALREADY TRACKED (since 7f8f1e33 and 14a729ae), so
# these entries change nothing on their own -- gitignore does not apply to
# tracked paths. They are recorded here so the intent is unambiguous, and so
# that IF a future commit untracks them the ignore is already in force. Making
# them take effect requires `git rm --cached`, which is NOT done on B5-0835
# (B5-0923 owns the tracked-root-litter untracking question).
/.qwen/
/.freebuff/

# Pene/ is a stray empty Windows %APPDATA% tree (AppData/Local/hermes/cache/
# scratch/b50765-fixtures) created by a tool run with a redirected APPDATA.
# It contains ZERO files, so git cannot see it at all and it was never at risk
# of being committed; the entry documents it and stops a future tool run that
# writes into it from making it sweep-able.
/Pene/

# Ledger backup at repo root (B5-0835, 2026-09-28). NOT deleted, see
# .agent/REPORTS/2026-09-28-Cline (space-bunny) b5-0835-B5-0835.md: measured
# to be a DIVERGED stale copy holding 0 unique task ids (388 bak rows, all 388
# present in the live ledger, and every one of the 17 differing lines is an
# older revision of a row the live ledger has since advanced past). It is a
# trap, not a recovery asset, but the row forbids deletion under either
# reading, so it is left on disk and only kept out of git.
/ledger.bak

# Stale local copy of the agent loop prompt (B5-0835, 2026-09-28). Diverged
# from .agent/AGENT_LOOP.md, which is the governed home: it still says "commit
# hash" in the STOP paragraph that the governed copy corrected to say the loop
# does not commit. Violates AGENTS.md section 6 (no new .md at repo root).
# Superseded, not canonical, so it is ignored rather than tracked.
/loop-prompt.md

# Fullwidth-colon lookalike directories at repo root (B5-0837, 2026-09-28).
# Two untracked trees whose names contain U+F03A (fullwidth colon, EF 80 BA):
# a 3-codepoint dir "dot-c + U+F03A" (len 3) materialised by an agent that
# resolved C:/temp/projects/Babylon5CCGGameDesign against the repo root, and
# a 19-codepoint dir "C + U+F03A + tempb5ccg-harness" (len 19, mtime
# 2026-09-27T10:30Z, empty). B5-0783 measured this hazard class: a fullwidth
# colon passes every Windows filename constraint, renders ambiguously across
# consoles, and normalises to the same key as ASCII. Contains (does not
# delete): deletion is a separate human-ratified action. The dir "dot-c +
# U+F03A" holds one displaced copy of the B5-0765 report (SHA256
# 2636A1D0327570AACC9180EFF07682438ABA9D9A4E1188F4750C3FD13A09516B, 5930b,
# mtime 2026-09-28T05:53:49Z) beside the canonical 5974b copy in
# .agent/REPORTS/ (SHA256 17941EAD5DB9B692844F6960F01F3C42E958EBEAB8F08B382FE769ADA3EE06CD),
# which is authoritative; the displaced copy is residue.
# Lines use U+F03A literally below; git treats it as an ordinary byte, not
# as a path separator (only ASCII 002F is a separator).
/.c
/Ctempb5ccg-harness

# Ten measured sweepable scratch artefacts (B5-0955, 2026-09-28). Each is
# untracked and un-ignored, so a plain `git add -A` checkpoint would absorb
# it; the row's disposition decision is IGNORE for every one and DELETE for
# none: the cited artefacts are measurement records other agents' reports
# point at (ocr-card/ocr-batch are the B5-0935/B5-0939 OCR instrumentation;
# tmp-0719-harness is cited by six files; TASK_LEDGER.md.bak is a diverged
# stale ledger copy, 0 unique ids, cited 8x, kept-only-out-of-git exactly
# like its already-ignored twin /ledger.bak at the root), the orb_*.py pair
# embodies the non-reproducible digit-template tuning the B5-0935 report
# recorded as a dead end, and deleting a 102-byte reproducible log
# (compile-b5-0925.log) buys nothing an ignore line does not, while an
# ignore line is reversible and a deletion of an untracked file is not.
/b5ccg/out_mer_slice/
/.agent/TASK_LEDGER.md.bak
/.agent/orb_digits.py
/.agent/orb_banner.py
/.agent/ocr-card.ps1
/.agent/ocr-batch.ps1
/.agent/tmp-0719-harness.ps1
/b5ccg/compile-b5-0925.log
/b5ccg/compile-b5-0935.log

# TRACKED files named by B5-0955 for completeness (belt-and-braces, same
# precedent as /.qwen/ above): gitignore does not apply to tracked paths, so
# these lines are INERT until the files are untracked (B5-0923/B5-0949 own
# that question). They are recorded so the intent is unambiguous and the
# ignore is already in force if untracking ever happens. A plain `git add -A`
# does not sweep tracked files regardless.
/b5ccg/compile-afterfix.txt
