# b5ccg gate output that is not build output: per-task compile logs (B5-0957,
# 2026-09-28). Named-scope, not /b5ccg/*.log: measured same-family logs that
# the narrower rule WOULD miss are compile-b5-0951.log (cited as a gate
# artifact by the DONE B5-0951 row note), compile-b5-0954.log and
# compile-b5-0956.log, all materialised mid-session while the seeding rows
# sat OPEN, so per-path lines rot exactly as fast as the queue generates
# logs. No *.log exists anywhere in the tracked tree outside
# .agent/SCOPE_RELEASES/ (run-queue dry-run captures, tracked deliberately),
# which is a DIFFERENT directory this rule does not touch.
/b5ccg/compile-*.log

# node_modules disposition (B5-0972, 2026-09-28): DECIDED gitignore-and-keep.
# This rule is the free half of the decision, taken without the human gate the
# row places on removal: it touches no tracked entry (all 67258 stay in the
# index until the human ratifies B5-0949's one-commit untrack), it is
# reversible by deleting this line, and it closes the real hazard today — a
# fresh `npm install` writing new files that a plain `git add -A` checkpoint
# would sweep. Tracked entries are unaffected by ignore rules (the /.qwen/
# precedent); once the ratified untrack lands, this rule becomes active
# immediately and no follow-up edit is needed. Removal itself is recorded as
# command-plus-rollback in .agent/REPORTS/2026-09-28-Buffy (glm-5.3-flash)-B5-0972.md
# and is NOT run here: `git rm` in any form stays behind the human gate.
/node_modules/

# Clock-integrity audit instrument (opencode (space-bunny-free) 7, 2026-09-30).
# Read-only PowerShell that scores every .agent/CLAIMS/*.json and
# .agent/HEARTBEATS/*.json on payload-vs-mtime, after excluding files whose mtime
# was bulk-assigned by one operation. It is the reproduction instrument cited by
# docs/reports/clock-integrity-in-agent-coordination-files-2026-09-30.md, whose
# §1 and §4.4 tables cannot be re-derived without it.
#
# IGNORE, do not delete -- the same disposition and the same reasoning as the
# /.agent/tmp-0719-harness.ps1 entry above (B5-0955): a cited measurement record
# is worth keeping on disk and worth keeping out of git, and an ignore line is
# reversible where deleting an untracked file is not.
#
# It was untracked and un-ignored when first written, which is a real hazard: a
# plain `git add -A` checkpoint absorbs it as though it were a deliverable, and
# the sibling probe dirs .agent/tmp_b51043/, .agent/tmp_b51104/ and
# .agent/tmp_b51113/ are untracked and un-ignored in exactly the same way at the
# time of writing. Those three are NOT listed here: they belong to other agents'
# closed tasks, so their disposition is theirs to record, not this line's to
# assume. See also docs/proposals/scratch-disposition-tmp-scans-proposal.md,
# which already owns part of that question.
# Machine-local scratch scans (B5-1405, 2026-10-01).
/tmp-scans/
/.agent/tmp_*
